    <!-- About and help -->
    <string name="acerca_de">About</string>
    <string name="acerca_de_texto">Tools to decrypt images encrypted with AES-256-GCM (.png.enc) and text encrypted with the Caesar cipher (.txt).\n\nEverything runs on this device and no result is saved: the temporary image is deleted when you leave the screen.</string>
    <string name="ayuda">Help</string>
    <string name="ayuda_aes_titulo">How to decrypt an image</string>
    <string name="ayuda_aes_texto">1. Tap «Import .png.enc file» and pick the encrypted file.\n2. Type the 16-character password (A-Z, a-z or 0-9) used to encrypt it.\n3. Tap «Decrypt» and wait for the progress bar to finish.\n4. The image appears in the preview. It is only shown on screen: it is not saved and is deleted when you leave.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_cesar_titulo">How to decrypt text</string>
    <string name="ayuda_cesar_texto">1. Tap «Import .txt» and pick the encrypted text file.\n2. Type the shift used to encrypt it, between 1 and 25.\n3. Tap «Decrypt»: the message appears on the right.\n\nIf the text does not make sense, try another shift.</string>
